module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.RelativeProjF1Functor

/-!
# Stacks 085D (1) on the constructed relative Proj of an algebraic space

In Situation 0849 let `P = Proj_X(𝒜)` be the relative homogeneous spectrum of Stacks 084A–084B,
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.RelativeProjSituation.relativeProjFunctor`, and suppose `𝒜` is generated
as an `𝒜₀`-algebra by `𝒜₁`. Stacks 085D (1): `P` represents the functor `F₁` of triples
`(f, ℒ, ψ)`. This file proves it for the constructed `P` and the functor
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.RelativeProjSituation.relativeProjF1Functor` of
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.RelativeProjF1Functor`.

## The hypothesis

A property of a quasi-coherent sheaf on an algebraic space is read on its étale charts: `𝒜` is
generated in degree one when its restriction `u^*𝒜` to every étale chart `u : U → X` is, as a
quasi-coherent graded algebra on the scheme `U` — over every affine open of `U` the ring of
sections is generated by its degree-one part over its degree-zero part, the hypothesis of the case
of schemes, Stacks 01O4 (`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjRepresentsF1.IsGeneratedInDegreeOne`).
That is `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.RelativeProjSituation.IsGeneratedInDegreeOneOnCharts`; the
restriction `u^*𝒜` is the library's restriction of `𝒜` to a scheme point,
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.RelativeProjSituation.pointAlgebra`. The source's hypothesis, read on
`𝒜` itself — over every affine étale chart of `X` the sections of `𝒜` are generated by those of
`𝒜₁` over those of `𝒜₀` — is `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.RelativeProjSituation.IsGeneratedInDegreeOne`
of `StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.RelativeProjF1Generated`, which implies this one.

## The proof

The source's proof is "see Constructions, Lemma 01O4 for the case of schemes". By
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.RelativeProjF1Functor` the natural map `F₁ ⟶ P` is injective
with no hypothesis; it remains to see that it is surjective at every test object `T`, that is,
that every section over `T` of `Proj_T(f^*𝒜) = T ×_X P` lies in the degree-one open `U₁` of
Tag 01NU, where the degree-one classifying morphism of Tag 01NZ is a bijection
(`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjQcohSheaf.Fd.degreeOpenEquiv`). So the content is
`U₁ = Proj_T(f^*𝒜)` for every scheme point `f : T → X`
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.RelativeProjSituation.degreeOpen_one_eq_top`):

* on an étale chart `u : U → X` this is the case of schemes
  (`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjRepresentsF1.degreeOpen_one_eq_top`), `u^*𝒜` being generated in
  degree one;
* the comparison morphism `Proj_{Z'}((g ∘ h)^*𝒜) ⟶ Proj_Z(g^*𝒜)` of the third assertion of
  Stacks 084B is cartesian and carries `U₁` into `U₁`, and the preimage of `U₁` is `U₁`
  (`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.RelativeProjSituation.exists_classifyingMorphism_comp_projComparison`
  and `...classifyingMorphism_comp_projComparison`, through the base-change morphism of Tag 01O3
  and the representation of Tag 01NZ); so `U₁ = Proj` passes to every base change, and descends
  along a surjective one;
* for an arbitrary `f`, the base change `T ×_X U ⟶ T` of an étale atlas `U ⟶ X` is surjective, and
  over `T ×_X U` the point `f` factors through the chart.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.RelativeProjSituation.IsGeneratedInDegreeOneOnCharts`: the hypothesis.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.RelativeProjSituation.relativeProjIsoF1`: Stacks 085D, part (1), the
  natural isomorphism `P ≅ F₁`, under the hypothesis on the étale charts; with the hypothesis on
  `𝒜` itself it is `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.RelativeProjSituation.relativeProjIsoF1OfGenerated`
  (`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.RelativeProjF1Generated`).

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 085D](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/085D)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 084B](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/084B)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01O3](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01O3)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01O4](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01O4)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite
open AlgebraicGeometry
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProj
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjBridge
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjQcohSheaf

universe u m

namespace Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjRepresentsF1

variable {S : Scheme.{u}} (A : SheafGradedAlgebra.{u} S) (P : RelativeProjData A)

/-- Every morphism into the degree-one open of Tag 01NU, followed by its inclusion, is a
degree-one classifying morphism. -/
theorem exists_classifyingHom_eq {W : Scheme.{u}} (n : W ⟶ (P.degreeOpen 1).toScheme) :
    ∃ ξ : Fd (situationAlgebra A) 1 W, classifyingHom A P ξ = n ≫ (P.degreeOpen 1).ι := by
  obtain ⟨ξ, hξ⟩ := Fd.homDegreeOpen_surjective A P Nat.one_pos W n
  exact ⟨ξ, congrArg (· ≫ (P.degreeOpen 1).ι) hξ⟩

/-- When the degree-one open of Tag 01NU is everything, every morphism into the relative
homogeneous spectrum is a degree-one classifying morphism. -/
theorem exists_classifyingHom_eq_of_eq_top (htop : P.degreeOpen 1 = ⊤) {W : Scheme.{u}}
    (m : W ⟶ P.scheme) : ∃ ξ : Fd (situationAlgebra A) 1 W, classifyingHom A P ξ = m := by
  obtain ⟨ξ, hξ⟩ := exists_classifyingHom_eq A P
    (m ≫ (P.scheme.isoOfEq htop ≪≫ P.scheme.topIso).inv)
  have hι : (P.scheme.isoOfEq htop ≪≫ P.scheme.topIso).hom = (P.degreeOpen 1).ι :=
    Scheme.isoOfEq_hom_ι P.scheme htop
  refine ⟨ξ, hξ.trans ?_⟩
  rw [← hι, Category.assoc, Iso.inv_hom_id, Category.comp_id]

/-- The degree-one open is everything as soon as every point of the relative homogeneous
spectrum is the image of a morphism factoring through it. -/
theorem degreeOpen_one_eq_top_of_forall {W : Scheme.{u}} (m : W ⟶ P.scheme)
    (n : W ⟶ (P.degreeOpen 1).toScheme) (hmn : m = n ≫ (P.degreeOpen 1).ι)
    (hm : Function.Surjective m.base) : P.degreeOpen 1 = ⊤ := by
  refine eq_top_iff.2 fun x _ => ?_
  obtain ⟨y, rfl⟩ := hm x
  have hy : m.base y ∈ Set.range (P.degreeOpen 1).ι.base := by
    rw [hmn]
    exact ⟨n.base y, rfl⟩
  rwa [Scheme.Opens.range_ι] at hy

end Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjRepresentsF1

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Space

namespace RelativeProjSituation

open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjRepresentsF1
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjInvertibleMorphism

variable (s : RelativeProjSituation.{u, m})

/-- **`𝒜` is generated as an `𝒜₀`-algebra by `𝒜₁`**, read on the étale charts of `X`: for every
étale chart `u : U → X` (an object of the small étale site of `X`), the restriction `u^*𝒜` of the
graded algebra to `U` is generated in degree one over every affine open of the scheme `U`, in the
sense of the case of schemes, Stacks 01O4. -/
def IsGeneratedInDegreeOneOnCharts : Prop :=
  ∀ V : SmallEtale s.site s.base s.containsBase s.space.1,
    IsGeneratedInDegreeOne (s.shrink.pointAlgebra V.obj.left V.obj.hom)

/-! ### The comparison morphism of Stacks 084B and the classifying morphisms -/

/-- **The comparison morphism of the third assertion of Stacks 084B on classifying morphisms.**
For `h : Z' ⟶ Z` and a point `x` of `F` of `(g ∘ h)^*𝒜` over a test scheme, the classifying
morphism of `x` followed by the comparison `Proj_{Z'}((g ∘ h)^*𝒜) ⟶ Proj_Z(g^*𝒜)` is the
classifying morphism of the base change along `h` of the transport of `x` to `h^*(g^*𝒜)`. -/
theorem classifyingMorphism_comp_projComparison {Z Z' : BigFppfOver s.site s.base s.containsBase}
    (g : yoneda.obj Z ⟶ s.space.1) (h : Z' ⟶ Z) {W : Scheme.{u}}
    (x : F (situationAlgebra (s.shrink.pointAlgebra Z' (yoneda.map h ≫ g))) W) :
    F.classifyingMorphism _ x ≫ (BigFppfOver.toScheme s.site s.base s.containsBase).map
        (s.quadrupleRestriction.projComparison s.shrink.contains_relativeProj_pointAlgebra g h) =
      F.classifyingMorphism (s.shrink.pointAlgebra Z g)
        (F.baseChangeUp ((BigFppfOver.toScheme s.site s.base s.containsBase).map h)
          (situationAlgebra (s.shrink.pointAlgebra Z g))
          (F.algebraTransport
            (unitalHomInverse (s.quadrupleRestriction.restrict h g _ rfl)
              (s.quadrupleRestriction.isIso_restrict_app h g _ rfl))
            (isIso_unitalHomInverse_app _ _) x)) := by
  have hκ := (s.isPullback_projComparison g h).2.2
  have h1 := F.classifyingMorphism_comp_relativeProjCongr
    (A₁ := s.shrink.pointAlgebra Z' (yoneda.map h ≫ g))
    (A₂ := (s.shrink.pointAlgebra Z g).pullback
      ((BigFppfOver.toScheme s.site s.base s.containsBase).map h))
    (s.quadrupleRestriction.restrict h g _ rfl)
    (s.quadrupleRestriction.isIso_restrict_app h g _ rfl)
    x
  have h2 := classifyingMorphism_baseChangeUp (s.shrink.pointAlgebra Z g)
    ((BigFppfOver.toScheme s.site s.base s.containsBase).map h)
    (F.algebraTransport
      (unitalHomInverse (s.quadrupleRestriction.restrict h g _ rfl)
        (s.quadrupleRestriction.isIso_restrict_app h g _ rfl))
      (isIso_unitalHomInverse_app _ _) x)
  refine (congrArg (F.classifyingMorphism _ x ≫ ·) hκ).trans ?_
  refine (Category.assoc _ _ _).symm.trans ?_
  exact (congrArg (· ≫ _) h1).trans h2.symm

/-- **Classifying morphisms into `Proj_Z(g^*𝒜)` over the image of `Z'` lift along the
comparison.** A class `x` over `a ≫ h` of `F` of `g^*𝒜` is, through the comparison, the
classifying morphism of a class over `a` of `F` of `(g ∘ h)^*𝒜` of the same degree. -/
theorem exists_classifyingMorphism_comp_projComparison
    {Z Z' : BigFppfOver s.site s.base s.containsBase}
    (g : yoneda.obj Z ⟶ s.space.1) (h : Z' ⟶ Z) {W : Scheme.{u}}
    (a : W ⟶ (BigFppfOver.toScheme s.site s.base s.containsBase).obj Z')
    (Q : Quadruple (a ≫ (BigFppfOver.toScheme s.site s.base s.containsBase).map h)
      (situationAlgebra (s.shrink.pointAlgebra Z g)) 1) :
    ∃ Q' : Quadruple a (situationAlgebra (s.shrink.pointAlgebra Z' (yoneda.map h ≫ g))) 1,
      F.classifyingMorphism _ (F.mk a one_pos Q') ≫
          (BigFppfOver.toScheme s.site s.base s.containsBase).map
            (s.quadrupleRestriction.projComparison
              s.shrink.contains_relativeProj_pointAlgebra g h) =
        F.classifyingMorphism _ (F.mk _ one_pos Q) := by
  set y := F.baseChangeDownQ ((BigFppfOver.toScheme s.site s.base s.containsBase).map h)
    (situationAlgebra (s.shrink.pointAlgebra Z g)) a
    (Quot.mk (UnionRel (f := a ≫ (BigFppfOver.toScheme s.site s.base s.containsBase).map h)
      (A := situationAlgebra (s.shrink.pointAlgebra Z g))) ⟨⟨1, one_pos⟩, Q⟩)
  obtain ⟨Q', hQ'⟩ : ∃ Q' : Quadruple a
      (situationAlgebra (s.shrink.pointAlgebra Z' (yoneda.map h ≫ g))) 1,
      F.mk a one_pos Q' = F.algebraTransport (s.quadrupleRestriction.restrict h g _ rfl)
        (s.quadrupleRestriction.isIso_restrict_app h g _ rfl) y := ⟨_, rfl⟩
  refine ⟨Q', ?_⟩
  rw [s.classifyingMorphism_comp_projComparison g h, hQ']
  congr 1
  exact (congrArg (F.baseChangeUp ((BigFppfOver.toScheme s.site s.base s.containsBase).map h)
    (situationAlgebra (s.shrink.pointAlgebra Z g)))
    ((F.algebraTransportEquiv _ _ _).symm_apply_apply y)).trans
    (F.baseChangeUp_baseChangeDownQ _ _ _ _)

/-- A degree-one classifying morphism into a relative homogeneous spectrum factors through the
degree-one open. -/
theorem classifyingMorphism_mk_eq {Y W : Scheme.{u}} (A : SheafGradedAlgebra.{u} Y) {g : W ⟶ Y}
    (Q : Quadruple g (situationAlgebra A) 1) :
    F.classifyingMorphism A (F.mk g one_pos Q) =
      Fd.homDegreeOpen A (relativeProj A) Nat.one_pos (Fd.mk g Q) ≫
        ((relativeProj A).degreeOpen 1).ι :=
  (classifyingHom_relativeProj_mk A Q).symm

/-! ### `U₁ = Proj` along the comparison morphisms of Stacks 084B -/

/-- **`U₁ = Proj` passes to base changes.** If the degree-one open of `Proj_Z(g^*𝒜)` is
everything, so is that of `Proj_{Z'}((g ∘ h)^*𝒜)`, for every `h : Z' ⟶ Z`: the identity of
`Proj_{Z'}((g ∘ h)^*𝒜)` lifts, through the cartesian comparison square of Stacks 084B, the
comparison morphism, which factors through `U₁`. -/
theorem degreeOpen_one_eq_top_comp {Z Z' : BigFppfOver s.site s.base s.containsBase}
    (g : yoneda.obj Z ⟶ s.space.1) (h : Z' ⟶ Z)
    (htop : (relativeProj (s.shrink.pointAlgebra Z g)).degreeOpen 1 = ⊤) :
    (relativeProj (s.shrink.pointAlgebra Z' (yoneda.map h ≫ g))).degreeOpen 1 = ⊤ := by
  have hsq := (s.quadrupleRestriction.isPullback_baseChangeHom_restrictProjIso
    s.shrink.contains_relativeProj_pointAlgebra g h).1
  obtain ⟨⟨g₀, q⟩, hξ⟩ := exists_classifyingHom_eq_of_eq_top _
    (relativeProj (s.shrink.pointAlgebra Z g)) htop
    ((BigFppfOver.toScheme s.site s.base s.containsBase).map
      (s.quadrupleRestriction.projComparison s.shrink.contains_relativeProj_pointAlgebra g h))
  induction q using Quotient.ind with
  | _ Q =>
  have hg₀ : g₀ = (relativeProj (s.shrink.pointAlgebra Z' (yoneda.map h ≫ g))).toBase ≫
      (BigFppfOver.toScheme s.site s.base s.containsBase).map h :=
    (classifyingHom_comp_toBase _ _ _).symm.trans ((congrArg (· ≫ _) hξ).trans hsq.w)
  subst hg₀
  obtain ⟨Q', hQ'⟩ := s.exists_classifyingMorphism_comp_projComparison g h _ Q
  have hQ'' := hQ'.trans ((classifyingHom_relativeProj_mk _ Q).symm.trans hξ)
  have hid : F.classifyingMorphism _ (F.mk _ one_pos Q') = 𝟙 _ := by
    refine hsq.hom_ext ?_ ?_
    · exact hQ''.trans (Category.id_comp _).symm
    · exact (F.classifyingMorphism_comp_toBase _ _).trans (Category.id_comp _).symm
  exact degreeOpen_one_eq_top_of_forall _ _ (𝟙 _) _ ((hid.symm.trans
    (classifyingMorphism_mk_eq _ Q'))) fun x => ⟨x, rfl⟩

/-- **`U₁ = Proj` descends along surjective base changes.** If `h : Z' ⟶ Z` is surjective and the
degree-one open of `Proj_{Z'}((g ∘ h)^*𝒜)` is everything, so is that of `Proj_Z(g^*𝒜)`: the
comparison morphism of Stacks 084B is surjective, being a base change of `h`, and it factors
through `U₁`. -/
theorem degreeOpen_one_eq_top_of_comp {Z Z' : BigFppfOver s.site s.base s.containsBase}
    (g : yoneda.obj Z ⟶ s.space.1) (h : Z' ⟶ Z)
    (hh : Surjective ((BigFppfOver.toScheme s.site s.base s.containsBase).map h))
    (htop : (relativeProj (s.shrink.pointAlgebra Z' (yoneda.map h ≫ g))).degreeOpen 1 = ⊤) :
    (relativeProj (s.shrink.pointAlgebra Z g)).degreeOpen 1 = ⊤ := by
  have hsq := (s.quadrupleRestriction.isPullback_baseChangeHom_restrictProjIso
    s.shrink.contains_relativeProj_pointAlgebra g h).1
  have hκ : Surjective ((BigFppfOver.toScheme s.site s.base s.containsBase).map
      (s.quadrupleRestriction.projComparison s.shrink.contains_relativeProj_pointAlgebra g h)) :=
    MorphismProperty.of_isPullback (P := @Surjective) hsq.flip hh
  obtain ⟨⟨g₀, q⟩, hξ⟩ := exists_classifyingHom_eq_of_eq_top _
    (relativeProj (s.shrink.pointAlgebra Z' (yoneda.map h ≫ g))) htop (𝟙 _)
  induction q using Quotient.ind with
  | _ Q' =>
  have e := s.classifyingMorphism_comp_projComparison g h (F.mk g₀ one_pos Q')
  have e' := ((congrArg (· ≫ _) ((classifyingHom_relativeProj_mk _ Q').symm.trans hξ)).symm.trans
    e).symm.trans (Category.id_comp _)
  exact degreeOpen_one_eq_top_of_forall _ _ _ _ (e'.symm.trans (classifyingMorphism_mk_eq _ _))
    hκ.surj

/-- **`U₁ = Proj_T(f^*𝒜)` at every scheme point**, when `𝒜` is generated in degree one on the
étale charts of `X`. On a chart it is the case of schemes; an arbitrary point `f : T → X` factors,
over the surjective base change `T ×_X U ⟶ T` of an étale atlas `U ⟶ X`, through the chart, and
`degreeOpen_one_eq_top_comp` and `degreeOpen_one_eq_top_of_comp` carry the equality there and
back. -/
theorem degreeOpen_one_eq_top (hgen : s.IsGeneratedInDegreeOneOnCharts)
    (T : BigFppfOver s.site s.base s.containsBase) (f : yoneda.obj T ⟶ s.space.1) :
    (relativeProj (s.shrink.pointAlgebra T f)).degreeOpen 1 = ⊤ := by
  obtain ⟨U, u, huS, huE⟩ := s.space.2.exists_atlas
  have hU : (relativeProj (s.shrink.pointAlgebra U u)).degreeOpen 1 = ⊤ :=
    Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjRepresentsF1.degreeOpen_one_eq_top _ _
      (hgen ⟨CostructuredArrow.mk u, huE⟩)
  have h1 := s.degreeOpen_one_eq_top_comp u (huE.rep.fst' f) hU
  have hpt : yoneda.map (huE.rep.fst' f) ≫ u = yoneda.map (huE.rep.snd f) ≫ f := by
    rw [huE.rep.map_fst']
    exact huE.rep.w f
  exact s.degreeOpen_one_eq_top_of_comp f (huE.rep.snd f) (huS.property_snd f)
    ((congrArg (fun k => (relativeProj (s.shrink.pointAlgebra _ k)).degreeOpen 1 = ⊤) hpt).mp h1)

/-! ### Stacks 085D (1) -/

variable (TA : TensorAlgebras.{u})

/-- **The morphism `F₁ ⟶ P` is surjective on points**, when `𝒜` is generated in degree one on
the étale charts of `X`: the section of `Proj_T(f^*𝒜)` attached to a `T`-point of `P` over `f`
lands in `U₁ = Proj_T(f^*𝒜)` (`degreeOpen_one_eq_top`), so it is a degree-one classifying
morphism, of a class of quadruples over the identity of `T`, which is the class of a triple. -/
theorem f1ToPoint_surjective (hgen : s.IsGeneratedInDegreeOneOnCharts)
    (T : BigFppfOver s.site s.base s.containsBase) :
    Function.Surjective (s.f1ToPoint TA (T := T)) := by
  intro v
  have hv : v ≫ s.relativeProjπ = yoneda.map (𝟙 T) ≫ (v ≫ s.relativeProjπ) := by
    rw [CategoryTheory.Functor.map_id, Category.id_comp]
  set σ := s.relativeProjPoints.pointEquivProjOver T (v ≫ s.relativeProjπ) (𝟙 T) ⟨v, hv⟩
  obtain ⟨⟨g₀, q⟩, hξ⟩ := exists_classifyingHom_eq_of_eq_top _
    (relativeProj (s.shrink.pointAlgebra T (v ≫ s.relativeProjπ)))
    (s.degreeOpen_one_eq_top hgen T (v ≫ s.relativeProjπ)) σ.1
  have hg₀ : g₀ = 𝟙 _ :=
    (classifyingHom_comp_toBase (s.shrink.pointAlgebra T (v ≫ s.relativeProjπ)) (relativeProj _)
      ⟨g₀, q⟩).symm.trans ((congrArg (· ≫ _) hξ).trans (σ.2.trans
        ((BigFppfOver.toScheme s.site s.base s.containsBase).map_id T)))
  subst hg₀
  obtain ⟨c, rfl⟩ := quadrupleClass_surjective (s.shrink.pointAlgebra T (v ≫ s.relativeProjπ)) TA
    (𝟙 _) q
  refine ⟨⟨v ≫ s.relativeProjπ, c⟩, ?_⟩
  have : (⟨classifyingHom (s.shrink.pointAlgebra T (v ≫ s.relativeProjπ)) (relativeProj _)
      ⟨𝟙 _, quadrupleClass _ TA _ c⟩, by
        rw [CategoryTheory.Functor.map_id]
        exact classifyingHom_comp_toBase _ _ _⟩ :
      {g : _ // g ≫ (relativeProj _).toBase = _}) = σ := Subtype.ext hξ
  exact congrArg Subtype.val
    ((congrArg (s.relativeProjPoints.pointEquivProjOver T (v ≫ s.relativeProjπ) (𝟙 T)).symm
      this).trans ((s.relativeProjPoints.pointEquivProjOver T _ (𝟙 T)).symm_apply_apply _))

/-- **Stacks 085D, part (1), on the constructed relative Proj, chart by chart.** For a
quasi-coherent graded `𝒪_X`-algebra `𝒜` on an algebraic space `X` whose restriction to every étale
chart is generated in degree one (`IsGeneratedInDegreeOneOnCharts`), the relative
homogeneous spectrum `P = Proj_X(𝒜)` constructed in Stacks 084A–084B represents the functor
`F₁` which sends `T` to the isomorphism classes of triples `(f, ℒ, ψ)`: `f : T → X`, `ℒ` an
invertible `𝒪_T`-module, and `ψ : f^*𝒜 ⟶ ⨁_{n ≥ 0} ℒ^{⊗ n}` a map of graded `𝒪_T`-algebras
inducing a surjection `f^*𝒜₁ ⟶ ℒ`.

`F₁` is `relativeProjF1Functor`, functorial by pullback of triples; the isomorphism is inverse to
the natural map `f1ToRelativeProj` sending a triple to the point of `P` it classifies (`P` is
lifted to the universe of `F₁`). `TA` is the choice of tensor algebras needed to write
`⨁_{n ≥ 0} ℒ^{⊗ n}`. Generation of `𝒜` itself as an `𝒜₀`-algebra by `𝒜₁` gives the hypothesis;
that is `relativeProjIsoF1OfGenerated` of
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.RelativeProjF1Generated`, the form registered for Stacks
085D (1). -/
def relativeProjIsoF1 (hgen : s.IsGeneratedInDegreeOneOnCharts) :
    s.relativeProjFunctor ⋙ uliftFunctor.{u + 1} ≅ s.relativeProjF1Functor TA :=
  (NatIso.ofComponents (fun T => Equiv.toIso (Equiv.ofBijective
      (fun x : s.F1Triples TA T.unop => ULift.up (yonedaEquiv (s.f1ToPoint TA x)))
      ⟨fun _ _ h => s.f1ToPoint_injective TA T.unop
          (yonedaEquiv.injective (congrArg ULift.down h)),
        fun y => by
          obtain ⟨x, hx⟩ := s.f1ToPoint_surjective TA hgen T.unop (yonedaEquiv.symm y.down)
          exact ⟨x, congrArg ULift.up ((congrArg yonedaEquiv hx).trans
            (yonedaEquiv.apply_symm_apply _))⟩⟩))
    (fun {_ _} τ => (s.f1ToRelativeProj TA).naturality τ)).symm

/-- The inverse of the isomorphism sends a triple to the point of `P` it classifies. -/
theorem relativeProjIsoF1_inv_app (hgen : s.IsGeneratedInDegreeOneOnCharts)
    (T : (BigFppfOver s.site s.base s.containsBase)ᵒᵖ) (x : s.F1Triples TA T.unop) :
    (s.relativeProjIsoF1 TA hgen).inv.app T x = ULift.up (yonedaEquiv (s.f1ToPoint TA x)) :=
  rfl

